  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"The population starts at \\\\(10\\\\) students and doubles after each completed month:\\n\\n- After 1 month: \\\\(10 \\\\times 2=20\\\\)\\n- After 2 months: \\\\(20 \\\\times 2=40\\\\)\\n- After 3 months: \\\\(40 \\\\times 2=80\\\\)\\n\\nEquivalently,\\n...\n- {\"content\":\"I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"A doubling means the population becomes twice its size at the start of that month. Starting with \\\\(10\\\\) students:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n10 \\\\xrightarrow{\\\\text{1 month}} 20\\n\\\\xrightarrow{\\\\text{2 months}} 40\\n\\\\xrightarrow{\\\\text{3 mont...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The population triples at the end of each month. Starting with 12 students:\n\n\\[\n\\text{End of May population}=12\\cdot 3^5=12\\cdot243=2916\n\\]\n\nThe number of additional students is:\n\n\\[\n2916-12=\\boxed{2904}\n\\]\n\nSo, **2,904 additional students** would have joined campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
